    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44770" root="&#xA;                        وهم&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            5
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَهَّمَ</span></b> 
                         is properly rendered <i>He presumed,
surmised, fancied,</i> or <i>supposed</i> a thing: and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَهُّمًا</span>, <i>upon presumption, surmise,</i> or <i>supposition;</i>
and <i>suppositively:</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَهْمٌ</span>; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالَ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَهَّمَ</span>
                        <i>He thought;</i> (S, K;) <i>he imagined</i> a thing: (TA:) <i>he doubted:</i> see an ex.,
in a verse of 'Antarah, cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَرَدَّمٌ</span>.

